        "raw": "<p>Taught the game to my friend, Ian, today. He&#39;s an experienced gamer, so our four-hero game against Blade in Inula Primalis was a cakewalk.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Afterwards, he seemd a bit lukewarm on the game -- that it was too easy, so we discussed doing a harder scenario and ended up using the same four heroes (Legacy, Ra, The Wraith, and Fanatic) versus Voss on Mars. In advanced mode.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>It was a slugfest. Ian made great use of Chastise -- keeping The Wraith alive while she used the Infrared Eyepiece to control what came out. A late Forced Deployment pulled out about a dozen minions, but very careful teamwork kept all of the heroes alive (albeit with a combined HP total of 7 amongst the four of them) and then a properly buffed Holy Nova cleared the board. The team triumphed in the next round. I don&#39;t recall it&#39;s name, but we got the story challenge where all the heroes were alive, but under 5 HP. (Down to the wire?)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>The best part? The game went on long enough that we were running out of time and trying to hurry through the later rounds. With a dozen villain cards in play, I was trying to work through the best way to deal with the two Guards in order to do the most damage to Voss. Ian then says, &#39;Trust me, Fanatic has this and will take out every minion, focus on other things&#39;. This from someone who was playing his second game ever. With no time to waste, I took the leap of faith ... and that&#39;s when Fanatic saved the day with Holy Nova.</p>",
